# Section 1 (PART1), side B T01: $6300-$72FF, loaded by LOAD_SECTION 1 (the intro, on a key: $699D).
# The code goes on in T02 ($7300): T02-T05 ($7300-$B2FF) are not in this meta yet.
source ../bin/b.T01.bin
include apple2io.sym
include game.sym
$0000 org $6300
$0000 code
$0000 label PART1
$0003 db 2
$0003 label SECTION_MARKS
$0003 note DISK_MARK ($6303) = SECTION_MARK[1], SIDE_MARK ($6304) = 1 (side B): checked by LOAD_SECTION
$0005 code
$0005 label START
@$6305 comment section 1's start: a new stack, the RNG seeded from the disk
@$6314 comment RND = the Disk II data latch EOR [$80]: the drive still spins after LOAD_SECTION's motor off,
@$6314 comment so the latch holds whatever nibble passes under the head. In the rehost DISK_SLOT16 is the boot
@$6314 comment slot: this reads the boot device's $C0nC.
@$6321 comment back to the resident bank 1
@$72FE note LDA $7E??,X: the instruction ends in T02 ($7300)
# section 1's variables and its animation tables ($634A-$63A9): the tables hold shape numbers, drawn by
# $0807 ($20 = X, $1F = Y, $21 = shape). One thing, at OBJ_X / OBJ_Y, is drawn in five parts ($65F2-$6711).
@$634A comment variables and animation tables: shape numbers for $0807 ($21), at X $20 / Y $1F
@$634A db 1
@$634A label OBJ_X
@$634A note X of the five-part thing drawn at $65F2 (what it is: not seen yet)
@$634B db 1
@$634B label OBJ_Y
@$634C db 1
@$634C label OBJ_STATE
@$634C note 0, 1, 2: picks how PART3 / PART4 animate ($667D, $66DA)
@$634D db 4
@$634D label PART1_SHAPES
@$634D note drawn at OBJ_X+$10, OBJ_Y+9
@$6351 db 1
@$6351 label PART1_FRAME
@$6351 note 0-3
@$6352 db 28
@$6352 label PART4_SHAPES
@$6352 note drawn at OBJ_X+$46, OBJ_Y-$0A
@$636E db 1
@$636E label PART4_FRAME
@$636E note 0-$1A; 8 in OBJ_STATE 1
@$636F db 12
@$636F label PART4_SHAPES_ALT
@$636F note instead of PART4_SHAPES while OBJ_TIMER is $16-$21, indexed by OBJ_TIMER-$16
@$637B db 9
@$637B label PART3_SHAPES
@$637B note drawn at OBJ_X+$38, OBJ_Y-9
@$6384 db 1
@$6384 label PART3_FRAME
@$6384 note up to 8 (then stays), down in OBJ_STATE 2
@$6385 db 1
@$6385 label OBJ_TIMER
@$6385 note counts up and down with OBJ_STATE ($6559-$65A2); $50 and over: PART3 frame 0
@$6386 db 4
@$6386 label PART2_SHAPES
@$6386 note drawn at OBJ_X+4, OBJ_Y-$0B
@$638A db 1
@$638A label PART2_FRAME
@$638A note 0-3
@$638B db 1
@$638B label VAR_638B
@$638C db 1
@$638C label VAR_638C
@$638D db 1
@$638D label VAR_638D
@$638D note $47 at the start
@$638E db 1
@$638E label UNUSED_638E
@$638F db 1
@$638F label RESTARTED
@$638F note 1: Y at T02's prompt ($7ACE), which jumps to RESTART: the opening animation is skipped ($64B0)
@$6390 db 1
@$6390 note FIXED_SHAPES-1: FIXED_FRAME 0 draws nothing
@$6391 db 14
@$6391 label FIXED_SHAPES
@$6391 note drawn at X $3F, Y $2B, indexed from 1 by FIXED_FRAME
@$639F db 1
@$639F label FIXED_FRAME
@$639F note 1-$0E
@$63A0 db 9
@$63A0 label SHAPES_63A0
@$63A0 note indexed by $39, drawn through $1BC0
@$63A9 db 1
@$63A9 label VAR_63A9
@$63A9 note a count down ($6914)
@$63AA label RESTART
@$63AA comment the section's (re)start: its variables to 0
rebase $6390 FIXED_SHAPES-1
